msgid ""
"3. Finding a product ID: go to Products → All products and point at the "
"product name; the ID is shown under it. The shortcode builder also lists "
"every donation product with its ID."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:48
msgid ""
"4. Slide height: make the slide at least as tall as the card (about 384 px "
"on every screen). The Compact card screen shows the card heights for "
"desktop, tablet and phone. To give every card one height, set --dp-compact-h "
"(and --dp-compact-h-md, --dp-compact-h-sm) on the slide."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:49
msgid ""
"5. Colors: Forms and appearance → Colors → Choose my own colors. Each color "
"field accepts a hex value or a CSS variable from your theme or page editor, "
"for example var(--brand), so the card follows your site palette."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:50
msgid ""
"6. If the slider moves on while a donor is halfway through, switch on "
"\"Start over when the card is hidden\". The compact card is only a look: how "
"the donor pays is set under Cart and checkout."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:51
msgid ""
"7. What the donor sees: through the cart the card has 2 steps (amount, then "
"details with \"Continue to checkout · amount\"); with direct donation it has "
"3 (amount, details, payment) and a thank-you. The step counter shows the "
"real number. A small lock line (\"Secure payment\") sits above the button; "
"you can switch it off under Compact card. With the Impact phrases module the "
"chosen amount's impact appears next to the amount; with the Tax relief "
"module the declaration shows its title and a short line, and \"Details\" "
"opens the full text inside the card."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:55
msgid "Open the Compact card settings"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:58
msgid "Turning on direct donation"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:60
msgid ""
"Direct donation is how the donor pays, not how the form looks: nothing is "
"added to the cart and the donor pays on WooCommerce's own payment page for "
"the order. It works with the centered window, side panel, bottom sheet, in-"
"page form and compact card."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:61
msgid ""
"For every product: Donation Panel → Cart and checkout → How donors pay → "
"switch on \"Skip the cart (direct donation)\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:62
msgid ""
"For one donation type: on the same screen choose \"Through the cart\" or "
"\"Direct (skip the cart)\" next to Fixed amount, Custom amount, Share-based, "
"Goal-based campaign or Products that offer an add-on donation. \"Use the "
"general setting\" follows the switch above."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:63
msgid ""
"For one product: Products → edit the product → Product data → Donation → "
"\"Skip the cart (direct donation)\". The line under it shows the current "
"value and where it comes from."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:64
msgid ""
"Order: the product setting wins, then the donation type, then the general "
"setting. A direct donation is a single-line order, so the add-on donation "
"choice is not shown when the result is direct."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:65
msgid ""
"On the compact card the payment page opens in a secure window. If a payment "
"method cannot work inside the window, the donor taps \"Open the payment page "
"instead\". Unpaid direct donations are cancelled automatically after the "
"WooCommerce stock hold time."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:69
msgid "Open How donors pay"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:74
msgid ""
"1. Give the product a goal: Products → edit the product → Product data → "
"Donation → goal amount. From then on the bar appears by itself in the "
"centered window, side panel, bottom sheet, in-page form and on the compact "
"card."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:75
msgid ""
"2. To show the bar on its own anywhere (a page, a sidebar, a slider), use "
"the shortcode below. Without an ID it finds the product it is placed in. Add "
"milestones=\"no\" or donors=\"no\" to hide those parts."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:76
msgid ""
"3. The real total only grows with paid orders and goes down after refunds or "
"cancellations. Items in a cart never change it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:77
msgid ""
"4. Donor's own gift: when a donor picks or types an amount, a lighter "
"striped part shows how far their gift would take the campaign, together with "
"the new total. After \"Add to cart\" it stays as \"in your cart\"; removing "
"it from the cart makes it disappear. Only that visitor sees it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:78
msgid ""
"5. After payment on the compact card the bar fetches the new total once, and "
"the donor's part becomes part of the real bar."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:79
msgid ""
"6. Settings: Donation Panel → Campaigns → Campaign progress bar. Switch off "
"the donor's own gift, the fill and count-up animation, or the small "
"celebration at the goal. Visitors who ask their device for less motion "
"always see the final values without animation."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:80
msgid ""
"7. Milestones on the shortcode bar (optional): a product custom field named "
"_donation_panel_milestones, one per line as percent = label, for example 50 "
"= Halfway. Developers can also use the donation_panel_milestones filter."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:81
msgid ""
"8. Shop, category and donation list cards: when the \"Donate\" button on a "
"card opens the form, the bar inside it works the same way (the donor's own "
"gift, cart, new total after payment). Nothing extra to set up; the bar files "
"load only when the donor reaches for the card of a product with a goal."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:85
msgid "Open the progress bar settings"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:88
msgid "For developers: filters"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:90
msgid ""
"donation_panel_convert_amount converts amounts for a multi-currency plugin. "
"donation_panel_amount_presets changes the quick amounts. "
"donation_panel_rest_controllers adds REST controllers. The full list with "
"examples is in docs/HOOKS.md in the plugin folder."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:95
msgid "What each module does"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:97
msgid ""
"Campaign: goal, amount raised and donor count. Impact: short equivalents "
"next to amounts. Social proof: totals only, never personal details."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:98
msgid ""
"Thank-you screen: a warm confirmation after the order. Tax relief: one "
"question; a yes saves name and address on the order. Donor account: sign-in, "
"My donations and give again. Side cart: a slide-in cart."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:99
msgid "A module that is switched off loads no code and no styles."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:104
msgid "Troubleshooting: the button does not show"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:106
msgid ""
"Check that the product is set up as a donation product (the Donation tab in "
"the product data box) and that it is published."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:107
msgid ""
"If your theme does not use the standard WooCommerce hooks, a fallback button "
"is drawn for you. If you place the shortcode or block yourself, only that "
"one appears: never two on the same page."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:108
msgid ""
"Still stuck? Place the shortcode in the product description or in a text "
"block. It works in any page editor."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:113
msgid "Multi-currency stores"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:115
msgid ""
"By default amounts are shown and charged in the active WooCommerce currency; "
"nothing is converted."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:116
msgid ""
"If you use a multi-currency plugin that needs conversion, a small adapter "
"snippet connects it through the documented donation_panel_convert_amount "
"filter. Ready-made snippets are in the plugin folder docs/site-snippets."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:121
msgid "Privacy and data protection"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:123
msgid ""
"Donor details (dedication, on-behalf-of name, phone, email) are saved on the "
"order exactly as typed. Orders, exports and erasure are handled by "
"WooCommerce and the WordPress privacy tools."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:124
msgid ""
"Write your privacy text on your own site. The plugin only shows a link under "
"the form."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:129
msgid "Phone number field"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:131
msgid ""
"1. Where it is: the phone number is part of the donor details step of the "
"donation form and of the compact card. There is nothing to set: the check "
"works for every country and language, on phones and computers."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:132
msgid ""
"2. What donors see: the country code list starts with your WooCommerce store "
"country. While typing, the number is spaced the way that country writes it "
"(for Turkey: 530 307 15 93) and no extra digits can be typed. A leading 0, "
"00 or country code (+90, +44) that is typed or pasted is removed by itself "
"and the country code list follows it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:133
msgid ""
"3. Wrong numbers: if the number is too short, a clear line appears under the "
"field when the donor leaves it, and the Continue button stays dimmed until "
"the number is complete. A number that does not look like a mobile number "
"(Turkey: not starting with 5, United Kingdom: not starting with 7) only "
"shows a hint and never blocks the gift. The same goes for countries whose "
"number lengths vary: a number of unusual length only shows a hint, and only "
"clearly impossible lengths are stopped."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:134
msgid ""
"4. What is saved: the donor details on the order keep the number exactly as "
"typed with its country code. The WooCommerce billing phone receives the same "
"number in international format (for example +905303071593), which payment, "
"SMS and shipping tools expect. The server checks the number again with the "
"same rules."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:139
msgid "Setting the colors"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:141
msgid ""
"1. Open Donation Panel → Forms and appearance → Colors. Under \"Use my theme "
"colors\" you see the two colors in use and where each one comes from: "
"\"Theme palette: primary\", \"Default\" or \"Follows the main color\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:142
msgid ""
"2. Which theme colors are used: only colors the theme names primary, brand, "
"accent, secondary, contrast or foreground (also numbered ones such as "
"accent-3). The main color must be readable on white; the button color must "
"keep its text readable. Nothing is guessed from other colors."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:143
msgid ""
"3. If the theme has no such names you see \"Colors could not be read from "
"your theme\" here and on the Overview. The form then uses a calm neutral ink "
"color until you choose your own."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:144
msgid ""
"4. To choose your own: select \"Choose my own colors\" and fill in Main "
"color and Button color. Each field takes a hex value (#12305A) or a CSS "
"variable from your theme or page editor, for example var(--brand). The line "
"under each field says what is used: \"Source: your choice.\" or, when empty, "
"the color that applies instead."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:145
msgid ""
"5. Button text turns black or white by itself so it stays readable (contrast "
"at least 4.5:1). Colors you choose are never changed by theme or plugin "
"updates."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:149
msgid "Open the Colors settings"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:154
msgid ""
"1. Turn it on: Donation Panel → Cart and checkout → Modules → Side cart. "
"After a gift is added, a basket slides in (a bottom sheet on phones) with "
"the gifts, the total and \"Complete donation\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:155
msgid ""
"2. Floating basket button: on the same screen under Side cart. It appears "
"only when the basket has a gift. Choose Bottom right or Bottom left so it "
"does not cover your chat or back-to-top button, or switch it off if your "
"theme shows its own cart icon."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:156
msgid ""
"3. A basket icon in your header: place the shortcode below in a header "
"widget or menu block. It shows the number of gifts and opens the same basket."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:157
msgid ""
"4. Extra gift suggestion: switch on \"Suggest an extra gift in the basket\", "
"enter the product ID (0 uses the add-on product) and up to three amounts "
"such as 50, 100. Donors add it with one tap; their details are taken from "
"the gift already in the basket."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:158
msgid ""
"5. The side cart never opens on the cart and checkout pages, and pages "
"without a donation form load none of its files."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/class-guide.php:162
msgid "Open the Side cart settings"
msgstr ""

